 "summary": "No upstream declaration replaces anything new here: Mathlib has only the coordinate-free `covarianceBilin` and a one-directional `ae_eq_integral_of_variance_eq_zero`, TauCeti's `covMatrix` is the matrix of a measure on `EuclideanSpace` (bridged both ways) and its `dotProduct_extend_zero` covers only the right factor. Existing API (`Matrix.toBilin'`, `toQuadraticForm'`, `polar_toQuadraticMap`, `covariance_fun_sum_fun_sum`, `PosSemidef.dotProduct_mulVec_zero_iff`, `isClosed_setOfPred_posSemidef`) is reused rather than reproved.",
